# fixedbugs, defect d-lane-blocking-small-2 (2026-11-24): the header a group
# names is a file, and the header it includes, `y.h`, is a link to a device,
# `/dev/null` (made in the case's copy, `links`). Defect 2572 refused a
# group's own header found so; one include below it, a FIFO hung `heroes
# build` in clang's first listing until it was killed, and a device was read
# as an empty header. Every file the opening and the groups' headers reach is
# now walked before any clang starts, and the group is refused with what
# stands where. A FIFO cannot be tracked by git, so the compiler's own tests
# hold that one (`cli/include_stands.hero`).

extern "x.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function x_one() -> i32

function main()
    print(x_one().to_str())
